{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "a18b518d-f74a-4864-bd76-2f3f2c693f02",
    "name": "Kavach server tests",
    "description": "Tests for the Kavach relay server.\n\n**Setup**\n- Collection → Variables → `baseUrl` = your server, e.g. `https://192.168.1.50:8443` (or `http://127.0.0.1:8099` for a local test run with ALLOW_INSECURE=1).\n- With the mkcert certificate: Postman → Settings → Certificates → CA certificates → ON, choose `rootCA.pem`. (Or Settings → General → SSL certificate verification OFF, for testing only.)\n- Run everything: right-click the collection → **Run collection**.\n\nThe server only ever sees encrypted blobs, so these tests check the web files, security headers, attacks that must fail, and (by hand) the WebSocket mailbox protocol.\n\n## WebSocket tests (Postman → New → WebSocket)\nPostman cannot put WebSocket requests inside an importable collection, so do these by hand. Variables from this collection work in the WebSocket tab.\n\n1. First run **1. Web app → Generate new test mailbox IDs** (makes `ridA`/`sidA`, `ridB`/`sidB`).\n2. New → **WebSocket**. URL: `wss://192.168.1.50:8443/ws` (with private server: `.../ws?k=YOUR_ACCESS_KEY`). Connect.\n3. Send these one by one (Message → JSON). Expected reply on the right.\n\n| # | Send | Expected reply |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `{\"op\":\"ping\",\"r\":1}` | `{\"op\":\"ok\",\"r\":1}` |\n| 2 | `{\"op\":\"new\",\"rid\":\"{{ridA}}\",\"r\":2}` | `{\"op\":\"ok\",\"r\":2,\"sid\":\"{{sidA}}\"}` |\n| 3 | `{\"op\":\"sub\",\"rid\":\"{{ridA}}\",\"r\":3}` | `{\"op\":\"ok\",\"r\":3,\"sid\":\"...\"}` |\n| 4 | `{\"op\":\"put\",\"sid\":\"{{sidA}}\",\"d\":\"hello-encrypted-blob\",\"r\":4}` | `{\"op\":\"ok\",\"r\":4}` then `{\"op\":\"msg\",\"sid\":\"...\",\"id\":\"XYZ\",\"d\":\"hello-encrypted-blob\"}` |\n| 5 | `{\"op\":\"ack\",\"rid\":\"{{ridA}}\",\"id\":\"XYZ\"}` (id from step 4) | nothing (message deleted from server) |\n| 6 | `{\"op\":\"ice\",\"r\":6}` | `{\"op\":\"ok\",\"r\":6,\"ice\":[...]}` (STUN/TURN servers) |\n| 7 | `{\"op\":\"del\",\"rid\":\"{{ridA}}\",\"r\":7}` | `{\"op\":\"ok\",\"r\":7}` and `{\"op\":\"gone\",...}` |\n| 8 | `{\"op\":\"put\",\"sid\":\"{{sidA}}\",\"d\":\"x\",\"r\":8}` | `{\"op\":\"err\",\"r\":8,\"e\":\"nobox\"}` (mailbox gone) |\n\n**Error checks**\n| Send | Expected |\n|---|---|\n| `not json` | `{\"op\":\"err\",\"e\":\"json\"}` |\n| `{\"op\":\"hack\",\"r\":9}` | `{\"op\":\"err\",\"r\":9,\"e\":\"op\"}` |\n| `{\"op\":\"new\",\"rid\":\"short\",\"r\":10}` | `{\"op\":\"err\",\"r\":10,\"e\":\"rid\"}` |\n| `{\"op\":\"new\",\"rid\":\"{{ridB}}\",\"r\":11}` twice | second: `{\"op\":\"err\",\"r\":11,\"e\":\"exists\"}` |\n| `{\"op\":\"rq\",\"g\":\"x\",\"pub\":\"k\",\"sid\":\"{{sidA}}\",\"r\":12}` | `{\"op\":\"err\",\"r\":12,\"e\":\"arg\"}` |\n| `{\"op\":\"rep\",\"r\":13}` | `{\"op\":\"err\",\"r\":13,\"e\":\"nomatch\"}` |\n\n**Two-tab test:** open a second WebSocket tab. In tab 1: `new` + `sub` with `ridB`. In tab 2: `put` to `sidB`. Tab 1 receives the message. This is exactly how two phones talk.\n\n**Private server:** with `ACCESS_KEY` set, connecting without `?k=` or with a wrong key must fail (401).\n",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
